<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Launcher icon for API 24–25, which is where minSdk sits.

  `adaptive-icon` is API 26+, so the sibling `mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml` is the
  *only* definition of this resource on older releases — meaning there was none, and
  Android 7.0/7.1 had no launcher icon to draw at all. Nothing warned about it: the
  build succeeds, lint stays quiet, and the APK simply ships with the icon missing on
  those devices.

  A layer-list of the same two pieces the adaptive icon uses, so the two cannot drift.
  The inset mirrors the safe zone an adaptive icon's foreground is drawn inside, which
  is what the foreground vector was authored against — without it the artwork renders
  edge-to-edge here and looks noticeably larger than on modern devices.

  Vector rather than the conventional per-density PNGs: it keeps one source of truth for
  the artwork. If a launcher on some old OEM skin renders it poorly, generating real
  PNGs into mipmap-{m,h,xh,xxh,xxxh}dpi is the fix — this file is then deleted, not
  edited.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@color/brand_navy" />
    <item
        android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground"
        android:inset="16.6%" />
</layer-list>
